From: Ze contributors
Subject: [PATCH] pppoe: take a session's source MAC from its port's hardware

vnet_pppoe_add_del_session read the encapsulating interface's hardware
through si->hw_if_index. A VLAN sub-interface is created from a zeroed
template (vnet_create_sub_interface), so that index is 0, local0, which
has no hardware address: a session on a VLAN access got source MAC
00:00:00:00:00:00, and every frame VPP encapsulated for it carried it.
vnet_get_sup_hw_interface resolves a sub-interface to its port's hardware.

Upstream: https://github.com/FDio/vpp at cbba0451bb0af02a3ab8e163f6f99062782258e6
(the same lookup is on master). Applies after ze/0103.

diff --git a/src/plugins/pppoe/pppoe.c b/src/plugins/pppoe/pppoe.c
--- a/src/plugins/pppoe/pppoe.c
+++ b/src/plugins/pppoe/pppoe.c
@@ -331,7 +331,10 @@
       if (a->encap_if_index == ~0)
         return VNET_API_ERROR_INVALID_SW_IF_INDEX;
       si = vnet_get_sw_interface (vnm, a->encap_if_index);
-      hi = vnet_get_hw_interface (vnm, si->hw_if_index);
+      /* A sub-interface's hw_if_index is not its port's: VLAN sub-interfaces
+       * come from a zeroed template. Its source MAC is the port's.
+       */
+      hi = vnet_get_sup_hw_interface (vnm, si->sw_if_index);
     }
 
   /* lookup session_table */
